{
  "id": "flujo-completo",
  "layout": "default",
  "masterId": "master-ssh",
  "sectionId": "conexion",
  "transition": "morph",
  "eyebrow": "09 · PRÁCTICA GUIADA",
  "title": "De cero a sesión remota en cinco movimientos.",
  "subtitle": "Avanzá por el flujo y comprobá cada resultado antes de seguir.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "Laboratorio: cliente → servidor",
      "items": [
        {
          "title": "1. Activar el servidor",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "terminal",
              "title": "servidor",
              "command": "sudo systemctl enable --now ssh",
              "output": "Servicio SSH activo"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "2. Obtener usuario e IP",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "terminal",
              "title": "servidor",
              "command": "whoami && hostname -I",
              "output": "ana\n192.168.1.42"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "3. Probar alcance",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "terminal",
              "title": "cliente",
              "command": "ping -c 3 192.168.1.42",
              "output": "3 packets transmitted, 3 received"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "4. Conectar",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "terminal",
              "title": "cliente",
              "command": "ssh ana@192.168.1.42",
              "output": "ana@servidor:~$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "5. Verificar y salir",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "terminal",
              "title": "sesión remota",
              "command": "hostname && whoami && exit",
              "output": "servidor\nana\nConnection closed."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "fragment": 0,
      "animation": "slide-up"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Usar los pasos como actividad: no avanzar si el resultado esperado no aparece.",
    "Ping puede estar bloqueado aunque SSH funcione; si falla, probar directamente el puerto con nc o Test-NetConnection."
  ]
}
